<Base title="Learning Site — publish lessons from your repository"><section class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">A desktop editor for learning websites</p><h1>Teach clearly.<br/><i>Publish</i> with ownership.</h1><p class="lede">Learning Site turns a Git repository into an approachable, maintainable course website—without giving up your files, your workflow, or your publishing destination.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button" href="/download/">Get the editor</a><a class="text-link" href="/docs/">Read the documentation →</a></div><div class="hero-grid"><div><b>Local first</b><span>Draft and preview before anything goes live.</span></div><div><b>Git native</b><span>Changes, history, recovery, and collaboration stay visible.</span></div><div><b>Deploy anywhere</b><span>Publish directly to GitHub Pages or Cloudflare Pages.</span></div></div></section><ReleaseCard /><section class="split"><div><p class="eyebrow">A calm publishing workflow</p><h2>From folder to finished course in one focused place.</h2></div><ol class="steps"><li><b>01</b><div><h3>Connect</h3><p>Start a new learning site or connect a repository you already trust.</p></div></li><li><b>02</b><div><h3>Shape</h3><p>Edit pages, organize media, choose a theme, and write in your own language.</p></div></li><li><b>03</b><div><h3>Publish</h3><p>Preview the result, sync Git, then send the static site to your host.</p></div></li></ol></section><section class="callout"><p class="eyebrow">Already use Learning Site?</p><h2>Your content has a path forward.</h2><p>The editor detects legacy projects, creates a Git recovery point, and upgrades safely while preserving your work.</p><a class="button light" href="/migration/">Read the migration guide</a></section></Base>
